# Best-effort network time.
#
# The journal's whole value is being able to say when something happened, and
# without this the appliance knows only what its RTC battery remembers. -n
# keeps busybox ntpd in the foreground for the supervisor, -N raises its
# priority, and -p names the servers. On a workshop network with no route to
# the internet this simply never succeeds, which costs a few packets and
# nothing else.
NTPD_OPTS="-n -N -p pool.ntp.org -p time.cloudflare.com"
